From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neanderfunk <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:50:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] information: a missing domain is not an error

gluonutil_get_domain() returns NULL on a single-domain firmware - there is
simply no domain to report. The collector returned -1 for that, and the daemon
logs every negative return at error level, so every node of every single-domain
community writes

    node-whisperer: Error collecting Information for id=4 name=domain code=-1

to the syslog on every round, forever. Measured on a Gluon v2023.2 node:
/lib/gluon/domains/ does not exist, gluon.core.domain is unset, and site.json's
domain_code is empty.

Report -ENODATA instead and let the daemon skip such a source quietly. Real
collection failures keep their error message.
---
 src/daemon.c      | 8 ++++++++
 src/information.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/daemon.c b/src/daemon.c
index b636150..ecdcc8c 100644
--- a/src/daemon.c
+++ b/src/daemon.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 
 #include "node-whisperer.h"
 #include "daemon.h"
@@ -85,6 +86,13 @@ static int nw_daemon_create_vendor_element_buf(struct nw *instance) {
 			log_error("Too much Information for id=%d name=%s",
 				  information_sources[i].type, information_sources[i].name);
 			return -ENOMEM;
+		} else if (ret == -ENODATA) {
+			/* Not applicable on this node - not an error. Skip quietly,
+			 * otherwise a single-domain firmware logs an error for the
+			 * domain source on every round, forever. */
+			log_debug("No Information applicable for id=%d name=%s",
+				  information_sources[i].type, information_sources[i].name);
+			continue;
 		} else if (ret < 0) {
 			/* Error */
 			log_error("Error collecting Information for id=%d name=%s code=%d",
diff --git a/src/information.c b/src/information.c
index 91dcc7f..c6e3ca5 100644
--- a/src/information.c
+++ b/src/information.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 
 #include <arpa/inet.h>
 #include <linux/unistd.h>
@@ -176,7 +177,10 @@ int node_whisperer_information_domain_collect(uint8_t *buffer, size_t buffer_siz
 
 	dom = gluonutil_get_domain();
 	if (!dom) {
-		ret = -1;
+		/* Not a multi-domain firmware: there is simply no domain to
+		 * report. -ENODATA tells the caller to skip this source quietly
+		 * instead of logging an error on every single round. */
+		ret = -ENODATA;
 		goto out_free;
 	}
 
